{"path":"3/library/types.html","title":"types — Dynamic type creation and names for built-in types","description":"Source code: Lib/types.py","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"anchor","id":"module-types"},{"type":"anchor","id":"types-dynamic-type-creation-and-names-for-built-in-types"},{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"types"},{"type":"text","value":" — Dynamic type creation and names for built-in types"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source code:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/python/cpython/tree/3.14/Lib/types.py","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lib/types.py"}]}]},{"type":"thematic_break"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This module defines utility functions to assist in dynamic creation of new types."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It also defines names for some object types that are used by the standard Python interpreter, but not exposed as builtins like "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#int","title":"int","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"int"}]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/stdtypes.html#str","title":"str","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"str"}]},{"type":"text","value":" are."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finally, it provides some additional type-related utility classes and functions that are not fundamental enough to be builtins."}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"dynamic-type-creation"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dynamic Type Creation"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"types.new_class","term":[{"type":"text","value":"types.new_class("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"name"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"bases"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"()"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"kwds"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"exec_body"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a class object dynamically using the appropriate metaclass."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The first three arguments are the components that make up a class definition header: the class name, the base classes (in order), the keyword arguments (such as "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"metaclass"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"exec_body"}]},{"type":"text","value":" argument is a callback that is used to populate the freshly created class namespace. It should accept the class namespace as its sole argument and update the namespace directly with the class contents. If no callback is provided, it has the same effect as passing in "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"lambda ns: None"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Added in version 3.3."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"types.prepare_class","term":[{"type":"text","value":"types.prepare_class("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"name"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"bases"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"()"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"kwds"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Calculates the appropriate metaclass and creates the class namespace."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The arguments are the components that make up a class definition header: the class name, the base classes (in order) and the keyword arguments (such as "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"metaclass"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The return value is a 3-tuple: "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"metaclass, namespace, kwds"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"metaclass"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is the appropriate metaclass, "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"namespace"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is the prepared class namespace and "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"kwds"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is an updated copy of the passed in "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"kwds"}]},{"type":"text","value":" argument with any "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'metaclass'"},{"type":"text","value":" entry removed. If no "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"kwds"}]},{"type":"text","value":" argument is passed in, this will be an empty dict."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Added in version 3.3."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changed in version 3.6: The default value for the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"namespace"},{"type":"text","value":" element of the returned tuple has changed. Now an insertion-order-preserving mapping is used when the metaclass does not have a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"__prepare__"},{"type":"text","value":" method."}]}]}]},{"type":"admonition","kind":"seealso","title":"See also","children":[{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html#metaclasses","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Metaclasses"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Full details of the class creation process supported by these functions"}]}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"anchor","id":"index-0"},{"type":"link","href":"https://peps.python.org/pep-3115/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"PEP 3115"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Metaclasses in Python 3000"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Introduced the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"__prepare__"},{"type":"text","value":" namespace hook"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"types.resolve_bases","term":[{"type":"text","value":"types.resolve_bases("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"bases"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resolve MRO entries dynamically as specified by "},{"type":"anchor","id":"index-1"},{"type":"link","href":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0560/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"PEP 560"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function looks for items in "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"bases"}]},{"type":"text","value":" that are not instances of "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#type","title":"type","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"type"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and returns a tuple where each such object that has an "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html#object.__mro_entries__","title":"object.__mro_entries__","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"__mro_entries__()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" method is replaced with an unpacked result of calling this method. If a "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"bases"}]},{"type":"text","value":" item is an instance of "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"type"},{"type":"text","value":", or it doesn’t have an "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"__mro_entries__()"},{"type":"text","value":" method, then it is included in the return tuple unchanged."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Added in version 3.7."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"types.get_original_bases","term":[{"type":"text","value":"types.get_original_bases("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"cls"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"/"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return the tuple of objects originally given as the bases of "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"cls"}]},{"type":"text","value":" before the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html#object.__mro_entries__","title":"object.__mro_entries__","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"__mro_entries__()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" method has been called on any bases (following the mechanisms laid out in "},{"type":"anchor","id":"index-2"},{"type":"link","href":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0560/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"PEP 560"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"). This is useful for introspecting "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#user-defined-generics","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generics"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For classes that have an "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"__orig_bases__"},{"type":"text","value":" attribute, this function returns the value of "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"cls.__orig_bases__"},{"type":"text","value":". For classes without the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"__orig_bases__"},{"type":"text","value":" attribute, "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html#type.__bases__","title":"type.__bases__","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"cls.__bases__"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is returned."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"python","code":"from typing import TypeVar, Generic, NamedTuple, TypedDict\n\nT = TypeVar(\"T\")\nclass Foo(Generic[T]): ...\nclass Bar(Foo[int], float): ...\nclass Baz(list[str]): ...\nEggs = NamedTuple(\"Eggs\", [(\"a\", int), (\"b\", str)])\nSpam = TypedDict(\"Spam\", {\"a\": int, \"b\": str})\n\nassert Bar.__bases__ == (Foo, float)\nassert get_original_bases(Bar) == (Foo[int], float)\n\nassert Baz.__bases__ == (list,)\nassert get_original_bases(Baz) == (list[str],)\n\nassert Eggs.__bases__ == (tuple,)\nassert get_original_bases(Eggs) == (NamedTuple,)\n\nassert Spam.__bases__ == (dict,)\nassert get_original_bases(Spam) == (TypedDict,)\n\nassert int.__bases__ == (object,)\nassert get_original_bases(int) == (object,)"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Added in version 3.12."}]}]}]},{"type":"admonition","kind":"seealso","title":"See also","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"anchor","id":"index-3"},{"type":"link","href":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0560/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"PEP 560"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Core support for typing module and generic types"}]}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"standard-interpreter-types"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Standard Interpreter Types"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This module provides names for many of the types that are required to implement a Python interpreter. It deliberately avoids including some of the types that arise only incidentally during processing such as the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"listiterator"},{"type":"text","value":" type."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Typical use of these names is for "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#isinstance","title":"isinstance","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"isinstance()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#issubclass","title":"issubclass","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"issubclass()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" checks."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you instantiate any of these types, note that signatures may vary between Python versions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Standard names are defined for the following types:"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"types.NoneType","term":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"class"},{"type":"text","value":" "}]},{"type":"text","value":"types.NoneType"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The type of "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/constants.html#None","title":"None","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"None"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Added in version 3.10."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"types.FunctionType","term":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"class"},{"type":"text","value":" "}]},{"type":"text","value":"types.FunctionType"}],"definition":[]},{"id":"types.LambdaType","term":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"class"},{"type":"text","value":" "}]},{"type":"text","value":"types.LambdaType"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The type of user-defined functions and functions created by "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/expressions.html#lambda","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"lambda"}]},{"type":"text","value":" expressions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Raises an "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/sys.html#auditing","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"auditing event"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"function.__new__"},{"type":"text","value":" with argument "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"code"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The audit event only occurs for direct instantiation of function objects, and is not raised for normal compilation."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"types.GeneratorType","term":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"class"},{"type":"text","value":" "}]},{"type":"text","value":"types.GeneratorType"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The type of "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/glossary.html#term-generator","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"generator"}]},{"type":"text","value":"-iterator objects, created by generator functions."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"types.CoroutineType","term":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"class"},{"type":"text","value":" "}]},{"type":"text","value":"types.CoroutineType"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The type of "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/glossary.html#term-coroutine","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"coroutine"}]},{"type":"text","value":" objects, created by "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/compound_stmts.html#async-def","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"async def"}]},{"type":"text","value":" functions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Added in version 3.5."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"types.AsyncGeneratorType","term":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"class"},{"type":"text","value":" "}]},{"type":"text","value